"\u003e\u003ch2 tabindex=\"-1\" class=\"heading-element\" dir=\"auto\"\u003eDeploy\u003c/h2\u003e\u003ca id=\"user-content-deploy\" class=\"anchor\" aria-label=\"Permalink: Deploy\" href=\"#deploy\"\u003e\u003csvg data-component=\"Octicon\" class=\"octicon octicon-link\" viewBox=\"0 0 16 16\" version=\"1.1\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" aria-hidden=\"true\"\u003e\u003cpath d=\"m7.775 3.275 1.25-1.25a3.5 3.5 0 1 1 4.95 4.95l-2.5 2.5a3.5 3.5 0 0 1-4.95 0 .751.751 0 0 1 .018-1.042.751.751 0 0 1 1.042-.018 1.998 1.998 0 0 0 2.83 0l2.5-2.5a2.002 2.002 0 0 0-2.83-2.83l-1.25 1.25a.751.751 0 0 1-1.042-.018.751.751 0 0 1-.018-1.042Zm-4.69 9.64a1.998 1.998 0 0 0 2.83 0l1.25-1.25a.751.751 0 0 1 1.042.018.751.751 0 0 1 .018 1.042l-1.25 1.25a3.5 3.5 0 1 1-4.95-4.95l2.5-2.5a3.5 3.5 0 0 1 4.95 0 .751.751 0 0 1-.018 1.042.751.751 0 0 1-1.042.018 1.998 1.998 0 0 0-2.83 0l-2.5 2.5a1.998 1.998 0 0 0 0 2.83Z\"\u003e\u003c/path\u003e\u003c/svg\u003e\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\n\u003cp dir=\"auto\"\u003eOne port: HTTP and \u003ccode\u003e/ws\u003c/code\u003e on 8770, loopback only. Dev stack: \u003ccode\u003emise run dev\u003c/code\u003e (or \u003ccode\u003edev:db\u003c/code\u003e,\n\u003ccode\u003edev:hub\u003c/code\u003e, \u003ccode\u003edev:tunnel\u003c/code\u003e; each calls \u003ccode\u003escripts/dev.sh _svc \u0026lt;name\u0026gt;\u003c/code\u003e), so no supervisor daemon is\nneeded. Production: systemd units in \u003ccode\u003eops/\u003c/code\u003e. The host opens no inbound ports. Provisioning,\nservice units, backups and the restore drill live in \u003ccode\u003eops/\u003c/code\u003e (\u003ccode\u003eops/README.md\u003c/code\u003e).\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp dir=\"auto\"\u003eDeploys install a prebuilt release asset instead of building on the host: tagging \u003ccode\u003evX.Y.Z\u003c/code\u003e\nruns \u003ccode\u003e.github/workflows/release.yml\u003c/code\u003e, which publishes \u003ccode\u003evtv-vX.Y.Z-linux-{x64,arm64}.tar.gz\u003c/code\u003e, and\n\u003ccode\u003emise.toml\u003c/code\u003e's \u003ccode\u003e[tools.\"http:vtv\"]\u003c/code\u003e tells mise how to fetch it. On the host:\n\u003ccode\u003ebash ops/deploy.sh --from-mise \u0026lt;version\u0026gt;\u003c/code\u003e (the build-from-source path stays as a fallback).\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp dir=\"auto\"\u003eRate limits, four buckets keyed on the client IP (the \u003ccode\u003eCF-Connecting-IP\u003c/code\u003e header when the tunnel\npeer is loopback, else the TCP peer):\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cmarkdown-accessiblity-table\u003e\u003ctable\u003e\n\u003cthead\u003e\n\u003ctr\u003e\n\u003cth\u003eBucket\u003c/th\u003e\n\u003cth\u003ePaths\u003c/th\u003e\n\u003cth\u003eRate\u003c/th\u003e\n\u003cth\u003eBurst\u003c/th\u003e\n\u003c/tr\u003e\n\u003c/thead\u003e\n\u003ctbody\u003e\n\u003ctr\u003e\n\u003ctd\u003eApi\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003ctd\u003e\u003ccode\u003e/api/*\u003c/code\u003e\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003ctd\u003e20/s\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003ctd\u003e40\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003c/tr\u003e\n\u003ctr\u003e\n\u003ctd\u003eAuth\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003ctd\u003e\u003ccode\u003e/auth/*\u003c/code\u003e\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003ctd\u003e5/s\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003ctd\u003e10\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003c/tr\u003e\n\u003ctr\u003e\n\u003ctd\u003eAdmin\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003ctd\u003e\u003ccode\u003e/admin/*\u003c/code\u003e\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003ctd\u003e5/s\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003ctd\u003e10\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003c/tr\u003e\n\u003ctr\u003e\n\u003ctd\u003eWs\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003ctd\u003e\u003ccode\u003e/ws\u003c/code\u003e (hosted mode only)\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003ctd\u003e10/s\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003ctd\u003e30\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003c/tr\u003e\n\u003c/tbody\u003e\n\u003c/table\u003e\u003c/markdown-accessiblity-table\u003e\n\u003cp dir=\"auto\"\u003eLoad test: \u003ccode\u003enode scripts/load_ws.mjs\u003c/code\u003e (60 concurrent sockets locally; the 1,000-socket target\nneeds several source IPs, tracked as DEBT-022).\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp dir=\"auto\"\u003eLaunch requirements: a public repository (the AGPL source offer on \u003ccode\u003e/notices.html\u003c/code\u003e points at it),\nthe data-terms review (Q2), the trademark review (Q3), and the privacy contact (Q9). CI: fmt,\nclippy, tests, audit, Rust-only contract job, both database engines; desktop installers on tags.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cdiv class=\"markdown-heading\" dir=\"auto\"\u003e\u003ch2 tabindex=\"-1\" class=\"heading-element\" dir=\"auto\"\u003eUI/UX\u003c/h2\u003e\u003ca id=\"user-content-uiux\" class=\"anchor\" aria-label=\"Permalink: UI/UX\" href=\"#uiux\"\u003e\u003csvg data-component=\"Octicon\" class=\"octicon octicon-link\" viewBox=\"0 0 16 16\" version=\"1.1\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" aria-hidden=\"true\"\u003e\u003cpath d=\"m7.775 3.275 1.25-1.25a3.5 3.5 0 1 1 4.95 4.95l-2.5 2.5a3.5 3.5 0 0 1-4.95 0 .751.751 0 0 1 .018-1.042.751.751 0 0 1 1.042-.018 1.998 1.998 0 0 0 2.83 0l2.5-2.5a2.002 2.002 0 0 0-2.83-2.83l-1.25 1.25a.751.751 0 0 1-1.042-.018.751.751 0 0 1-.018-1.042Zm-4.69 9.64a1.998 1.998 0 0 0 2.83 0l1.25-1.25a.751.751 0 0 1 1.042.018.751.751 0 0 1 .018 1.042l-1.25 1.25a3.5 3.5 0 1 1-4.95-4.95l2.5-2.5a3.5 3.5 0 0 1 4.95 0 .751.751 0 0 1-.018 1.042.751.751 0 0 1-1.042.018 1.998 1.998 0 0 0-2.83 0l-2.5 2.5a1.998 1.998 0 0 0 0 2.83Z\"\u003e\u003c/path\u003e\u003c/svg\u003e\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\n\u003cp dir=\"auto\"\u003eNew screens use only the hub theme variables from \u003ccode\u003ehub/theme.js\u003c/code\u003e (graphite, black, light presets), 3 to\n6 px radii, 12 px labels and 14 px text, one accent element per view. Contrast fixes measured from the\npresets: a derived \u003ccode\u003e--onAccent\u003c/code\u003e, error text in \u003ccode\u003e--text\u003c/code\u003e with a \u003ccode\u003e--bad\u003c/code\u003e icon, \u003ccode\u003e--dim\u003c/code\u003e input borders and\nhints. Design record: \u003ccode\u003e.paul/design/taste/hub-theme.md\u003c/code\u003e, \u003ccode\u003e.paul/design/polish-log.md\u003c/code\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cdiv class=\"markdown-heading\" dir=\"auto\"\u003e\u003ch2 tabindex=\"-1\" class=\"heading-element\" dir=\"auto\"\u003eDesign Decisions\u003c/h2\u003e\u003ca id=\"user-content-design-decisions\" class=\"anchor\" aria-label=\"Permalink: Design Decisions\" href=\"#design-decisions\"\u003e\u003csvg data-component=\"Octicon\" class=\"octicon octicon-link\" viewBox=\"0 0 16 16\" version=\"1.1\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" aria-hidden=\"true\"\u003e\u003cpath d=\"m7.775 3.275 1.25-1.25a3.5 3.5 0 1 1 4.95 4.95l-2.5 2.5a3.5 3.5 0 0 1-4.95 0 .751.751 0 0 1 .018-1.042.751.751 0 0 1 1.042-.018 1.998 1.998 0 0 0 2.83 0l2.5-2.5a2.002 2.002 0 0 0-2.83-2.83l-1.25 1.25a.751.751 0 0 1-1.042-.018.751.751 0 0 1-.018-1.042Zm-4.69 9.64a1.998 1.998 0 0 0 2.83 0l1.25-1.25a.751.751 0 0 1 1.042.018.751.751 0 0 1 .018 1.042l-1.25 1.25a3.5 3.5 0 1 1-4.95-4.95l2.5-2.5a3.5 3.5 0 0 1 4.95 0 .751.751 0 0 1-.018 1.042.751.751 0 0 1-1.042.018 1.998 1.998 0 0 0-2.83 0l-2.5 2.5a1.998 1.998 0 0 0 0 2.83Z\"\u003e\u003c/path\u003e\u003c/svg\u003e\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\n\u003col dir=\"auto\"\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eOne router, two hosts: the desktop app is a thin shell over the hosted site.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eHosted at vtradingview.com for public users; charts public, saved state behind Google sign-in.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eFrontend kept; existing response shapes are the contract.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eOne port: HTTP and websocket on 8770.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eGoogle only, auto login for returning users, account created on first sign-in; desktop signs in\nthrough the system browser and a \u003ccode\u003evtradingview://\u003c/code\u003e deep link.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eServer-side sessions, not JWT.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eSign-in merge: the server value wins, the local value is kept as a 30-day backup the user can restore.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003esqlx Postgres driver over pgsqlite by default; both engines tested in CI.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eKey-value \u003ccode\u003euser_state\u003c/code\u003e with versions; a stale save returns 409.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eMT5 through per-user HTTPS bridge URLs behind an SSRF guard; the bridge stays Python.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eLogs and restart are admin-only.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003emise tasks for the dev stack, systemd on the host, plus a new Cloudflare Tunnel.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003ePublic deploy (Phase 4) before sync, desktop and MT5.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003ePrimary metric: p75 time to first live candle under 2 s; guardrail: zero cross-user data exposure.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eNew screens in the existing hub theme (\u003ccode\u003ehub-native\u003c/code\u003e), text one step above the chart chrome.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ol\u003e\n\u003cdiv class=\"markdown-heading\" dir=\"auto\"\u003e\u003ch2 tabindex=\"-1\" class=\"heading-element\" dir=\"auto\"\u003eImplementation Phases\u003c/h2\u003e\u003ca id=\"user-content-implementation-phases\" class=\"anchor\" aria-label=\"Permalink: Implementation Phases\" href=\"#implementation-phases\"\u003e\u003csvg data-component=\"Octicon\" class=\"octicon octicon-link\" viewBox=\"0 0 16 16\" version=\"1.1\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" aria-hidden=\"true\"\u003e\u003cpath d=\"m7.775 3.275 1.25-1.25a3.5 3.5 0 1 1 4.95 4.95l-2.5 2.5a3.5 3.5 0 0 1-4.95 0 .751.751 0 0 1 .018-1.042.751.751 0 0 1 1.042-.018 1.998 1.998 0 0 0 2.83 0l2.5-2.5a2.002 2.002 0 0 0-2.83-2.83l-1.25 1.25a.751.751 0 0 1-1.042-.018.751.751 0 0 1-.018-1.042Zm-4.69 9.64a1.998 1.998 0 0 0 2.83 0l1.25-1.25a.751.751 0 0 1 1.042.018.751.751 0 0 1 .018 1.042l-1.25 1.25a3.5 3.5 0 1 1-4.95-4.95l2.5-2.5a3.5 3.5 0 0 1 4.95 0 .751.751 0 0 1-.018 1.042.751.751 0 0 1-1.042.018 1.998 1.998 0 0 0-2.83 0l-2.5 2.5a1.998 1.998 0 0 0 0 2.83Z\"\u003e\u003c/path\u003e\u003c/svg\u003e\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\n\u003cmarkdown-accessiblity-table\u003e\u003ctable\u003e\n\u003cthead\u003e\n\u003ctr\u003e\n\u003cth\u003e#\u003c/th\u003e\n\u003cth\u003ePhase\u003c/th\u003e\n\u003cth\u003eDone when\u003c/th\u003e\n\u003c/tr\u003e\n\u003c/thead\u003e\n\u003ctbody\u003e\n\u003ctr\u003e\n\u003ctd\u003e1\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003ctd\u003eRust workspace, \u003ccode\u003ehub-server\u003c/code\u003e parity\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003ctd\u003econtract suite passes against Python and Rust\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003c/tr\u003e\n\u003ctr\u003e\n\u003ctd\u003e2\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003ctd\u003eOrder flow in Rust\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003ctd\u003egolden fixtures match within tolerance\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003c/tr\u003e\n\u003ctr\u003e\n\u003ctd\u003e3\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003ctd\u003eDatabase and Google sign-in\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003ctd\u003esign-in creates one user; CI green on pgsqlite and Postgres 17\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003c/tr\u003e\n\u003ctr\u003e\n\u003ctd\u003e4\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003ctd\u003ePublic deploy\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003ctd\u003elive through the tunnel, no inbound ports, backup restore drill done\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003c/tr\u003e\n\u003ctr\u003e\n\u003ctd\u003e5\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003ctd\u003eSynced state\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003ctd\u003ea layout drawn signed-out appears after sign-in in a second browser\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003c/tr\u003e\n\u003ctr\u003e\n\u003ctd\u003e6\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003ctd\u003eTauri desktop\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003ctd\u003einstalled app signs in via the system browser, same layout\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003c/tr\u003e\n\u003ctr\u003e\n\u003ctd\u003e7\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003ctd\u003ePer-user MT5 bridges\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003ctd\u003ea bridge streams for its owner; every SSRF case refused\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003c/tr\u003e\n\u003c/tbody\u003e\n\u003c/table\u003e\u003c/markdown-accessiblity-table\u003e\n\u003cdiv class=\"markdown-heading\" dir=\"auto\"\u003e\u003ch2 tabindex=\"-1\" class=\"heading-element\" dir=\"auto\"\u003eReview Status\u003c/h2\u003e\u003ca id=\"user-content-review-status\" class=\"anchor\" aria-label=\"Permalink: Review Status\" href=\"#review-status\"\u003e\u003csvg data-component=\"Octicon\" class=\"octicon octicon-link\" viewBox=\"0 0 16 16\" version=\"1.1\" width=\"16\" h